{ { … a_place_to_stay_curious:

Lead the product direction and delivery of customer-facing crypto experiences for the Crypto Frontend team at DKB Code Factory. You’ll turn product goals and user needs into clear priorities, working closely with UX, engineering, QA, and business stakeholders. You’ll validate ideas before development, coordinate releases, and measure whether delivered features create customer and business value.

} } ;

{ your_responsibilities: [

• Own and evolve the product roadmap, making priorities, milestones, and cross-team dependencies clear to stakeholders.

• Maintain a prioritized backlog. Ensure stories have clear acceptance criteria, meet the Definition of Ready, and support roadmap objectives.

• Lead discovery with UX and engineering through user research, prototyping, and experiments to validate problems and solutions before development.

• Drive delivery of customer-facing features; define success measures and ensure usage and outcome data can be tracked.

• Coordinate release planning and cross-team dependencies, and improve delivery predictability and throughput.

• Reduce rework and time to value through clearer requirements, earlier validation, and close collaboration with engineering and QA.

• Use data to balance customer value, business goals, technical sustainability, and compliance considerations.

] } ;

{ following_qualifications_would_be_in_line_with_our_desired_profile_for_this_position: [

• 3–7+ years’ experience as a Product Owner, Product Manager, Business Analyst, or in a similar software product delivery role.

• Experience working in agile teams (Scrum and/or Kanban), with strong backlog management, prioritization, and refinement skills.

• Experience owning product roadmaps and coordinating cross-team dependencies and releases.

• Strong user story writing and acceptance criteria skills.

• Experience leading discovery and partnering with UX and engineering to validate solutions.

• An analytical mindset, including experience defining product KPIs and using analytics to inform decisions.

• Strong stakeholder management and communication skills; comfortable working with international, cross-functional teams.

• Fluent written and spoken English. German is a plus

• Experience with API-driven software environments and familiarity with regulatory or compliance considerations in banking or financial services.

• You're passionate about your work, but also know how to enjoy your free time!

] } ;

Got the feeling not to match every single requirement? Don’t worry! We encourage you to apply anyways, even if your qualifications do not align perfectly. You might still be just the right candidate for us!

